my $CODE = <<'END_CODE';
hello world
foo bar hello baz
END_CODE

{
    desc => q{?pattern searches backward for a pattern},
    description => <<'END_DESC',
## Macro: `xt/visual/macros/search_backward`

**?pattern** searches backward through the buffer for the given pattern. From line 2, `?hello` wraps backward to find "hello" on line 1.

**Keys:** `j` then `?hello\n`

**initial.png**
- Cursor at line 1, col 0
- Text has "hello" on lines 1 and 2

**after_move_down.png**
- Cursor at line 2, col 0 (moved down with `j`)

**after_search_backward.png**
- Cursor on "hello" on line 1, col 0
- Search highlights visible on both "hello" occurrences
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('j');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_move_down');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('?hello\n');
        $ctx->delay(300);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_search_backward');
    },
}
